.TH tkulayoutcanvas n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkulayoutcanvas
.PP
Visual block layout designer on a Tk canvas. Place named blocks on a paper\-sized page in millimetres, snap to a grid, toggle visibility, and edit geometry in a built\-in side panel. Backend: \fBtclutils::tulayout\fR.
.PP
Designed for a \fBcoarse\fR layout step (block positions and visibility). Fine tuning (columns, fonts, PDF overlay) stays in the host application.
.SS API
.CS
::tkutils::tkulayoutcanvas::widget $path ?options?
::tkutils::tkulayoutcanvas::configure $path ?-option value ...?
::tkutils::tkulayoutcanvas::cget $path -option
::tkutils::tkulayoutcanvas::getBlocks $path
::tkutils::tkulayoutcanvas::setBlocks $path $blocks
::tkutils::tkulayoutcanvas::select $path $blockId
::tkutils::tkulayoutcanvas::getCanvas $path
::tkutils::tkulayoutcanvas::redraw $path
::tkutils::tkulayoutcanvas::mergePreset $path $presetDict ?-keys {x y w show}?
.CE
.SS "Options (creation and \fBconfigure\fR)"
.TS
l l l.
Option	Default	Meaning
\fB\-paper\fR	\fBa4\fR	Paper name (\fBa4\fR, \fBa5\fR, \fBletter\fR)
\fB\-orientation\fR	\fBportrait\fR	\fBportrait\fR or \fBlandscape\fR
\fB\-margin\fR	\fB20.0\fR	Page margin in mm (drawn as dashed rect)
\fB\-gridmm\fR	\fB5.0\fR	Snap grid in mm
\fB\-scale\fR	\fB3.0\fR	Pixels per mm on the canvas
\fB\-blocks\fR	\fB{}\fR	Block dict (id → block)
\fB\-definitions\fR	\fB{}\fR	Catalog dict: default label/size for each id
\fB\-blockorder\fR	\fB{}\fR	Explicit draw/list order (else from definitions)
\fB\-onchange\fR	\fB{}\fR	Callback: \fBcmd $path $blocks\fR after drag/edit
\fB\-showgrid\fR	\fB1\fR	Draw mm grid
\fB\-properties\fR	\fB1\fR	Show list + spinboxes panel
\fB\-width\fR / \fB\-height\fR	\fB640\fR / \fB480\fR	Initial canvas size
.TE
.SS Interaction
.IP \(bu
Click a block on the canvas or in the list to select it.
.IP \(bu
Drag a block; coordinates snap to \fB\-gridmm\fR.
.IP \(bu
Auto\-Y blocks (\fBy==0\fR or \fBlockedY 1\fR) show a grey dashed preview, keep \fBy\fR at \fB0\fR, and only move horizontally when dragged.
.IP \(bu
Spinboxes and the \fBVisible\fR checkbutton update the block dict and fire \fB\-onchange\fR.
.SS "Minimal example"
.CS
package require tkutils::tkulayoutcanvas

set defs {
    title {label Title w 160 h 12}
    body  {label Body  w 160 h 50}
}
set blocks {
    title {label Title x 25 y 30 w 160 h 12 show 1}
    body  {label Body  x 25 y 55 w 160 h 50 show 1}
}

tkutils::tkulayoutcanvas::widget .lc -blocks $blocks -definitions $defs \
    -onchange {apply {{p b} {
        puts "layout changed: [dict size $b] blocks"
    }}}
pack .lc -fill both -expand 1
.CE
.SS Demo
.CS
wish examples/demo-tkulayoutcanvas.tcl
# or
wish bin/tkulayoutcanvas.tcl
.CE
.SS Tests
.CS
tclsh tests/tkulayoutcanvas.test
# headless: xvfb-run -a tclsh tests/tkulayoutcanvas.test
.CE
.SS "Integration guide"
.PP
See \fBdocs/HANDOFF\-layout\-designer.md\fR for how a host app (e.g. a document editor) wires presets, handoff files, and \fBmergeBlocks\fR.
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB{TKUTILS TKULAYOUTCANVAS NOWIDGET|OPTION|EXISTS|BLOCK}\fR
